* Sun Oct 04 2026 Juhani Lehtimäki <juhani.lehtimaki@iki.fi> - 0.5.0-1
- Harpoon puts itself on the list on first start, so it keeps itself up
  to date. If you stop tracking it, it is not added again.
- An app's address can be changed in its settings, for example when its
  repository moves to another forge. Harpoon checks the new address first
  and keeps the app's settings, name and installed version.
- App settings are also in the list's long-press menu.
- The cover no longer says "No apps tracked" while apps are tracked.

* Sat Oct 03 2026 Juhani Lehtimäki <juhani.lehtimaki@iki.fi> - 0.4.2-1
- The three layers of the animated sea each drift at their own, slower
  pace, so the waves have depth without drawing the eye.
- The "No builds yet" notice on an app's page no longer touches the waves.

* Sat Oct 03 2026 Juhani Lehtimäki <juhani.lehtimaki@iki.fi> - 0.4.1-1
- Apps whose repository has no builds yet can be added: Harpoon shows
  them as waiting for builds, explains why, and offers them as soon as
  the developer publishes a release with packages.
- Clearer errors: a Codeberg/Forgejo repository with Releases turned off
  is no longer reported as "Repository not found"; the message says what
  is wrong, links the developer's website and tells developers how to fix
  it. "No releases" and "no package for this phone" explain the fix too.

* Sat Oct 03 2026 Juhani Lehtimäki <juhani.lehtimaki@iki.fi> - 0.4.0-1
- The app list looks finished with only a few apps: a status header that
  says where things stand ("All caught up", "2 updates ready"), when apps
  were last checked, an "Add another app" row, a tip card, and the sea
  along the bottom.
- Adding an app: one-tap github.com, codeberg.org and codefloe.com
  shortcuts, and "Paste link" when a link is on the clipboard.
- A failed add brings the form back as it was, with the error, so a typo
  is fixed instead of retyped; "Add it anyway" adds an app that has no
  release yet.

* Sat Oct 03 2026 Juhani Lehtimäki <juhani.lehtimaki@iki.fi> - 0.3.0-1
- A fresh look: artwork of a harpoon over the sea in the colours of your
  ambience, a bobbing harpoon when the list is empty, an "updates ready"
  band that installs everything with one tap, status icons on the list,
  a hero header on each app's page with "What's new" first, and a new
  About page.
- Settings pages are tidied: icons on the main switches and one aligned
  style for all explanations.
- The QR scanner's camera preview is no longer turned sideways.

* Sat Oct 03 2026 Juhani Lehtimäki <juhani.lehtimaki@iki.fi> - 0.2.0-1
- Release notes are shown formatted, with working links; the app page
  shows the app's icon and download size; app settings show the
  essentials first, with the rest behind "Show advanced settings".
- Build provenance: Sigstore bundles logged to Rekor v2 (with RFC 3161
  timestamps) are verified on the phone, and an app can require that its
  builds were signed by a given workflow or from given branches or tags.
- Correctness and security fixes from a code review: multi-package apps
  are tracked and removed as a whole, installs of one app never overlap
  with the background job, rpm is never handed an option-like name,
  downloads are size-limited, and redirects to other hosts drop
  credentials.
- Faster: one rpm call at start, and rpm no longer blocks the UI when an
  app changes.
- Release packages for SailfishOS 5.0 (sfos5.0) and 5.1 or later
  (sfos5.1), for aarch64, armv7hl and i486.

* Sat Oct 03 2026 Juhani Lehtimäki <juhani.lehtimaki@iki.fi> - 0.1.2-1
- Fixes from the second device test: the background check now fires on
  its own (the drop-in no longer clears the startup triggers), the
  background job no longer reports failure for apps whose check failed
  nor runs the fallback check twice, its notifications show as Harpoon's,
  apps already installed are recognised when added, harpoon-cli set
  re-checks the app, provenance messages name the package and show
  lists the result, and long package names wrap cleanly.

* Fri Oct 02 2026 Juhani Lehtimäki <juhani.lehtimaki@iki.fi> - 0.1.1-1
- Fixes from the first device test on SailfishOS 5.1: files are no longer
  created world-writable under the app launcher (umask), the background
  check now runs when the timer is started after boot, the QR scanner page
  loads (QtMultimedia 5.6), English plural forms, clearer status for apps
  whose check failed, a hint for projects that publish RPMs only inside
  archives, the cover counts failed checks, smaller layout fixes, and
  stripped, position-independent binaries.

* Fri Oct 02 2026 Juhani Lehtimäki <juhani.lehtimaki@iki.fi> - 0.1.0-1
- First release: track apps on GitHub, Codeberg/Forgejo/Gitea, GitLab,
  SourceHut, SourceForge, Jenkins, web pages, direct links and rpm-md
  repositories; install and update them through PackageKit or the system
  installer; background checks with notifications and optional automatic
  updates; backups; add apps by scanning a QR code or opening a
  harpoon://add link, and share them as QR codes; GitHub build provenance
  checked with local Sigstore verification.
